    "title": "AP-101 Treatment for ALS: Facts from AD/PD™ 2026 Conference",
    "text": "• AP-101 is an investigational human-derived antibody therapeutic.\n• AP-101 selectively targets the misfolded, toxic form of SOD1.\n• The aim of AP-101 is to disrupt the progressive spread of ALS.\n• Results supporting AP-101 were presented at the AD/PD™ 2026 International Conference on Alzheimer’s and Parkinson’s Diseases.\n• The results are supported by neuroaxonal injury biomarkers pNfH and NfL after six months of treatment.\n• Preparations are underway to advance AP-101 into a confirmatory Phase 3 clinical trial.\n• The Phase 3 clinical trial is planned to begin in late 2026.",
